From eb8ce6d40b8a76399431b89f68fb690acdfb5063 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hugo Evans <hugoevans92@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:05:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui): add Button size="touch" for 44px mobile CTAs

The Figma library in #803 draws Button size=touch and lists this as a
P0 follow-up. Code repeated size="lg" plus a className="h-11" override
on fifteen buttons, so Code Connect could not map 1:1.

- Add size="touch" (44px) to the Button cva; lg stays 36px.
- Move the fifteen size="lg" + h-11 buttons to size="touch" with no
  visual change.
- Move the lg CTAs that rendered at 36px to size="touch" so they meet
  the 44px target: Continue (access form), Retry sign out and Try again
  (sign-in shell), Retry loading memes (invest category), and the
  copy-address button (add money).
- Leave the savings vault picker row (Item rendered as a Button) and
  primary navigation (owns its own min-h-11) on lg.
- Add a Sizes story and a design-system note.

Checks: typecheck, oxlint, gates, bun test (2011 pass, 0 fail) and the
Storybook build all pass. The Sizes story renders touch at 44px.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
